{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>באשמורת הבוקר</b> (at the morning watch) — twice here, and the other: ויבאו בתוך המחנה באשמורת הבוקר, regarding Saul's battle against the men of Jabesh-gilead — for it is a time of favor, when the Holy One, blessed be He, performs a miracle for the righteous." "<b>וישקף</b> (And He looked out) — four times here, and the other: וישקף על פני סדום — just as there they were judged with fire and brimstone, so were they judged here. וישקף אבימלך, וישקף ארונה וירא את המלך — just as Abimelech was king of the Philistines, so was Aravnah a king, as written: את הכל נתן ארונה המלך למלך." "<b>ויהם</b> (And He threw into panic) — twice in the Masorah, and the other: ויהם ה' את סיסרא — to say: just as here the pillar of cloud would descend and dampen the ground, making it mud, and the pillar of fire would boil it, and the hooves of their horses would slip — so was it with Sisera; and just as there the brook Kishon swept them away, so here the sea cast them onto dry land."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:56.705654363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}